{
  "_about": "Persona and memories, eighth try, the last v1 tweak (2026-10-26). g26m7 (one memory at a time, no meet-ups, trained silence after unanswered nudges) was lively and declined false memories, but said 'I don't recall' to anything (half its training refusals began that way, weighted 24) and once took the caller's job as its own. g26m8: memory mentions as a spread (about 30% of persona calls none, 50% one, 20% two, each after the caller talks); refusals in varied words (the writer gets two of 14 examples per call; the 280 earlier refusals rewritten, rephrase_refusals.py); the memories are the caller's, never the friend's; 300 new persona calls; lighter memory weights (10/3, recall 6/2); learning rate eased off to 10% by the end (cosine); 64 calls held out for a validation loss every 50 steps, to see whether 600 steps is too few or too many.",
